{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.ColorCurveQPartials","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCurveQPartials","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QDifferenceOperator","lean:module:QOU.Mass.ColorCurveQIntegerForm"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCurveQPartials.qPartialZ_on_curve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCurveQPartials.qPartialZ_on_curve","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCurveQPartials.lean#L61-L69","doc":"**The branch-selection defect.** On the curve `C_z(X) = 0`, the z-partial collapses\nto `Δ_q^{z} C(X,z) = C_{qz}(X)` — the (generically nonzero) measure of how far `X` fails\nto remain a root under `z ↦ qz`. Its vanishing would require `X` to be simultaneously a\nroot over `z` and `qz`; the correction to a genuine root `X_q` of `C_{qz}` is the branch\ndatum the q-difference prolongation must choose. This is the precise remaining W1\nobstruction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCurveQPartials.qPartialZ_colorCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCurveQPartials.qPartialZ_colorCubic","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCurveQPartials.lean#L53-L59","doc":"**q-partial in `z`** (holding `X`): `Δ_q^{z} C_z(X) = (q−1)z·X² +\n((q²−1)z²+(q−1)z)·X + ((q³−1)z³+(q²−1)z²+(q−1)z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.ColorCurveQPartials.qPartialX_colorCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.ColorCurveQPartials.qPartialX_colorCubic","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/ColorCurveQPartials.lean#L45-L51","doc":"**q-partial in `X`** (holding `z`): `Δ_q^{X} C_z(X) = (q³−1)X³ + (q²−1)(z+1)X²\n+ (q−1)(z²+z+1)X`. Each degree-`k` term picks up `q^k − 1` (the monomial action). ","signatureChunk":0}]}